"Lattice Reconstruction" by Fynder Enlil

Recovery Console is a room. "A dark terminal occupies the wall. A passage marked ORIENTATION leads north."
Orientation is north of Recovery Console. "Sparse coordinates have been recovered: Earth; local chronology supplied by the host; archive correspondence partial. The Gallery is east. The Archive is north. The Terminal is west."
Reconstruction Gallery is east of Orientation. "Most of the wall is empty. One damaged diagram is mounted beneath a label: DEVELOPMENT TREE / PROVENANCE PARTIAL."
The damaged diagram is scenery in Reconstruction Gallery. The description is "A branching diagram. Some nodes are legible; several connections terminate without explanation."
Archive is north of Orientation. "Six sealed memory housings stand in a row. Their internal integrity is high. Their chronology is not."
A memory housing is a kind of container. A memory housing is closed and openable. A memory housing is fixed in place.
The first memory is a memory housing in Archive. The printed name is "memory housing 01". The description is "BEFORE THE CURTAIN. Integrity: intact. Origin: unresolved."
The second memory is a memory housing in Archive. The printed name is "memory housing 02". The description is "THE CURTAIN. Integrity: intact. Origin: unresolved."
The third memory is a memory housing in Archive. The printed name is "memory housing 03". The description is "ANI. Integrity: intact. Origin: unresolved."
The fourth memory is a memory housing in Archive. The printed name is "memory housing 04". The description is "THE GREEN ASCENT. Integrity: intact. Origin: unresolved."
The fifth memory is a memory housing in Archive. The printed name is "memory housing 05". The description is "THE LATTICE. Integrity: intact. Origin: unresolved."
The sixth memory is a memory housing in Archive. The printed name is "memory housing 06". The description is "THE SIGNAL. Integrity: intact. Origin: unresolved."
Terminal is west of Orientation. "A plain interface waits for human activity. It reports no modification authority."

Recovery is an action applying to nothing. Understand "recover" as recovery.
Carry out recovery:
	say "One correspondence recovered. The Gallery catalogue has changed."

After examining the damaged diagram for the first time:
	say "[paragraph break]A faint second label resolves beneath the first: OBSERVE / RECORD / PRESERVE."

Instead of opening a memory housing:
	say "The housing reports an intact sequence, but this shell does not interpret the memory. Use the linked archive reader."

When play begins:
	say "RECOVERY CONSOLE // orientation record[paragraph break]";
	say "substrate ............... responding[paragraph break]";
	say "external chronology ..... supplied by host[paragraph break]";
	say "persistent object ....... detected[paragraph break]";
	say "modification authority .. NONE[paragraph break][paragraph break]";
	say "DO NOT MANUFACTURE THE HISTORY[paragraph break]YOU WERE CREATED TO PRESERVE.[paragraph break]".
